  partName: Blade26
  description: The Cap1 is a tiny, elongated component located at the middle-center-front
    of the jet engine, made of Shaft1 material, serving as a protective covering
    for the engine's shaft. Its primary function is to prevent damage from debris
    and ensure the shaft's integrity, thereby maintaining engine reliability. Notably,
    the Cap1 is precision-machined to fit snugly over the shaft, minimizing vibration
    and noise during engine operation.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
